laurel 2160: the caller's own pages as GPU buffers (request 0x49), port of negroni 0232 to the topaz RedwoodGPU; stage-1 tables only.
Why: without it a process that uses Metal's newBufferWithBytesNoCopy: fails, and m2vtest's import step (0x6505) can never pass, so
/usr/libexec/laurel-metal-gate could never widen the clients ("LAUREL GPU SMMU: on" boots too). The pages stay wired while the handle
lives; cleaned at import and at each submission that names them; never kept; no user mapping through the connection. RedwoodGPU's
NegroniGPUABI now names "userptr" (Turnip's stand-in asks the kernel only then). One line: LAUREL GPU HOST PAGES: on|off. Kill switch
gpu_hostimport=0. Design: docs/laurel_sprout/metal.md section 6.2.

